  "symptom": "After movement, simulation realtime factor falls and display/control feel delayed.",
  "root_cause": "The mass-weighted speed projection uses small dense linear solves. NumPy OpenBLAS selected 16 threads by default, introducing severe scheduling overhead when speed limits become active.",
  "unchanged_physics": "Same repaired ONNX, PD/contact settings, discrete integrator and speed-projection algorithm. The numerical thread comparison used the same recorded poses and mass matrices.",
  "changes": [
    "Only ELF4 ExecuteProcess sets OPENBLAS_NUM_THREADS=1, OMP_NUM_THREADS=1 and MKL_NUM_THREADS=1 before Python imports NumPy.",
    "Viewer uses a private model/data and dedicated latest-state worker; sync and forward do not hold the physics/command lock.",
    "Only explicit GUI pose/equality edits and fresh mouse forces merge back; generation rejects stale reset results and forces expire after 200 ms.",
    "ROS observation messages are built under lock and published outside it.",
    "Camera snapshots copy the complete integration state rather than full MjData, and RGB/depth queues retain one latest frame."
